From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: entry lookups, multicast/path/stack tables, initialisers, owner modules, SendARP

- GetIpForwardEntry2, GetIpNetEntry2, GetMulticastIpAddressEntry and
  GetAnycastIpAddressEntry were unexported stubs. They now look the row up in
  the corresponding table by interface (index or LUID, one of the two is
  required) and key, fill in the rest of the row, and return ERROR_NOT_FOUND
  or ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER like the documented behaviour.
- GetMulticastIpAddressTable reports the all-hosts groups every IP interface
  joins (224.0.0.1; ff01::1 and ff02::1 with interface and link scope).
  GetIpPathTable/GetIpPathEntry report the empty path cache.
  GetIfStackTable and GetInvertedIfStackTable return the sorted (0,n)/(n,0)
  rows of interfaces with nothing stacked above or below them.
- InitializeIpForwardEntry and InitializeUnicastIpAddressEntry set the
  "unspecified" values; GetIpErrorString returns the ping texts for
  IP_STATUS 11001-11050 with the size counting the NUL.
- Get/SetSessionCompartmentId and Set/GetCurrentThreadCompartmentId model the
  single primary compartment, with no FIXME noise.
- GetOwnerModuleFrom{Tcp,Tcp6,Udp,Udp6}Entry and ...PidAndInfo return the
  basic module info (name, full path) of the owning process in the caller's
  buffer; SendARP resolves our own addresses from the interface and others
  from the neighbour table after provoking the system to ask.
- Headers: TCPIP_OWNER_MODULE_*, MIB_MULTICASTIPADDRESS_*, MIB_IFSTACK_*,
  MIB_INVERTEDIFSTACK_*, MIB_IPPATH_* and the prototypes.

Gate: test/iphlpapient-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/iphlpapient-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_IPE_* (iphlpapi/entries.c).
